@dgozman I didn't think I can make an isolated reproduction but here is:
https://github.com/kryaksy/playwright-digest-do-not-match-repro
It also contains the report from the latest reproduction in case you couldn't reproduce it in your environment. I hope it works though.

@kryaksy The problem here is [this `test.use()` call](https://github.com/kryaksy/playwright-digest-do-not-match-repro/blob/master/src/fixtures/index.ts#L45). Because it is in a shared fixtures file, it is only executed during the first `require()` of that file (`dummy.spec.ts`), so the use overrides apply to the first test file that required the fixtures, but not the others. Unfortunately, that leads to some internal inconsistency in the test runner, which I will look into.

For now, I'd suggest to move `test.use()` into `test.extend()`:
```ts
export const myTest = base.extend<Fixtures>({
  // add fixtures here
  // ....

  // add use options here
  viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 },
  trace: { mode: "on", snapshots: true },
  video: { mode: "on", size: { width: 1920, height: 1080 } },
});
```
